agent-ops task task-0546bfdd-803f-4dce-9787-93ff76c8f9ce: 1.0 compatibility policy and fail-closed surface discovery (M2, M3, M4)
criteria:
- discovery-git-failure: When any git command in surface discovery fails (ls-files, rev-parse or diff exits non-zero, or a git grep exits other than 0 or 1, including termination by a signal), the surface gate returns NOT_RUN SURFACE_DISCOVERY_FAILED whose details name the failed command (and the query for grep); review exits 1 with code SURFACE_DISCOVERY_FAILED and reason surface-discovery-failed instead of passing, verify prints its advisory line naming that code, and a rerun after the git problem clears searches again rather than reusing a failed result.
- derived-cap-visible: When a derived query kind (diff tokens, template fragments, hunk-header names) has more than 400 queries, the review packet's surface discovery (seen by both rounds) lists the dropped count per source, the second-round reviewer prompt states how many derived queries of which source were never searched, and verify prints a stdout advisory line 'Surface: N derived queries were not searched (<source> <count>, ...)'; at 400 or fewer per kind nothing is listed and no such line or prompt text appears.
- untracked-derived: In worktree-mode discovery (no --base), the content of untracked regular files in the change scope (ignored files are never in that scope) yields derived queries like added lines, so a sibling of a token that appears only in a new untracked file blocks as SURFACE_UNCLASSIFIED; a file containing a NUL byte, a symlink or other non-regular entry, and a file that no longer exists are skipped, any other read error returns SURFACE_DISCOVERY_FAILED naming the path, and --base discovery is unchanged.
- compat-guide: docs/en/guides/compatibility.md and its zh-TW mirror state the 1.0 compatibility policy: guaranteed interfaces, excluded interfaces, gate-change rules (minor; security fixes may be patch; removing or renaming a documented code is major), deprecation (at least one minor with a stderr warning, removal only in a major), migration (newer 1.x reads older 1.x config and state, no downgrade), support (latest 1.x minor; dropping an end-of-life Node release is a minor) and platform and host tiers; both languages have the same section count and the same backticked identifiers, and README Project status and SECURITY Supported versions link to the guide.
- gate-docs: Both languages of the acceptance-and-evidence spec name SURFACE_DISCOVERY_FAILED, the reported derived-query cap and untracked-file extraction, and the CHANGELOG Unreleased section has a Gate: entry for each of the three changes.
